Z||000000||CanadianGT||04-18-2001||06:23 PM||||Hi,<BR>I was wondering if anyone has any experience with the supercharger that rsm sells here in Toronto for the 2.8.  It says you will get 200h/p at the wheels on a stock motor.  If you stay at the boost they recomend for that ( I think 9psi) should you get an engine rebuild first, or will it be ok as is?<BR>Thanks<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||04-18-2001||08:32 PM||||I hear they've had probs. with the charger<BR>but that's just what I heard.<BR>I KNOW they have shipped sveral of my fellow club members (in IL.) the wrong parts.<BR>If you're set on forced induction I would suggest using the turbo as it has been used by MANY Fiero owners with great results.<BR>That's just my opinion of though. ;-)<P>If your engine has 60,000 or less you can probably get away with it but if more then<BR>it would be a good idea to get the rebuild.<BR>If you rebuild, keep the comp. ratio at 8.5:1<BR>or even less to avoid doing it all over. :-)<BR>Also; if you do rebuild you can add some other mods to even get more power!<BR>Check out:http://members.nbci.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm<BR>This guy can give you some info too.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||kslish||04-18-2001||11:20 PM||||I know someone that has an RSM Supercharger on their 2.8 and it has been troubleprone.  He has the original design from RSM that uses a Rotrex supercharger unit.  The Rotrex doesn't seem to hold up that well (internal oiling problems with the gear drive) if driven hard (and isn't that the point?).  RSM now sells their kit with a Vortech supercharger so maybe that has solved the reliability problem.  <P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> ||||reg||1
